research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals.log-6-BOUNDARY: The proof correctly handles all boundary conditions. The codomain (0,∞) is non‑empty and excludes 0 (positivity from L2). For any y>0 (including y=1, where exp(0)=1) the limits at ±∞ from L2 give a strict bracket exp(a)<y<exp(b) with a<b. Continuity on the closed interval [a,b] follows from L1, so the IVT (L3) supplies a point c without any choice principle. The constructive nature of the IVT is respected, and no degenerate or empty cases apply.
