research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals.result.json:16:  "tail": "VERDICT: CLEAN\n\nBOUNDARY: The proof correctly handles all boundary conditions. The codomain (0,∞) is non‑empty and excludes 0 (positivity from L2). For any y>0 (including y=1, where exp(0)=1) the limits at ±∞ from L2 give a strict bracket exp(a)<y<exp(b) with a<b. Continuity on the closed interval [a,b] follows from L1, so the IVT (L3) supplies a point c without any choice principle. The constructive nature of the IVT is respected, and no degenerate or empty cases apply.\n\nSOURCES: The full text of all four declared dependencies was inspected: `thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing` (provides strict increase and continuity), `thm-exponential-limits-and-range` (provides positivity, limits, and unboundedness), `thm-intermediate-value` (provides the IVT), and `cor-power-series-sums-are-continuous` (provides continuity of the power series, redundant here but correctly cited). Each statement exactly matches the usage in the target’s proof.\n\nCHECKED: Title, public claim (the bijection statement), every numbered step (1.1, 1.2, 2.1), and Remarks (none) were examined. The inferences are logically valid and mathematically accurate."
