research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log:42488: {"id":"thm-exponential-product-limit","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_logandexp.html","https://people.math.wisc.edu/~hkeisler/foundations.pdf"],"rationale":"Lebl Exercise 5.4.5 states e^x=lim_n(1+x/n)^n for every real x, with the same eventual-domain convention implicit in a real sequence. The library supplies a binomial head-tail proof instead of Lebl's logarithmic hint.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-42489- {"id":"thm-picard-iterates-for-exponential","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_picard.html","https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~ancoop/3600/section-34.html"],"rationale":"Lebl's Picard example for y'=y, y(0)=1 gives the iterates 1+x+...+x^n/n! and their global limit exp. The item additionally records compact-uniform convergence and the limiting integral equation, so it is a faithful strengthened packaging; its induction and interchange proof adapt the standard construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-42490- {"id":"thm-exponential-definition-equivalence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~ancoop/3600/section-34.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_picard.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_logandexp.html"],"rationale":"The sources identify the ODE, factorial power series, product-limit, functional-equation, and Picard descriptions of the ordinary exponential across their sections. The item is a library-specific consolidation of five standard characterizations, and its proof is the local composition of the preceding equivalence results.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
