research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-57451- {"id":"thm-exponential-ivp-uniqueness","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch10.pdf","https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~ancoop/3600/section-34.html"],"rationale":"Hunter Proposition 10.25 and the Penn notes characterize exp as the unique differentiable solution of f'=f with f(0)=1. The local integrating-factor proof is a standard adaptation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-57452- {"id":"thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.tamu.edu/~yvorobets/MATH409-2013C/Lect2-07web.pdf","https://math.mit.edu/~stevenj/exponential.pdf"],"rationale":"The Texas A&M notes give uniqueness of the continuous positive multiplicative function normalized at 1, and Johnson derives exponential form from continuity of a nonzero multiplicative solution. The item combines that standard characterization with the differentiability-at-zero normalization F(0)=F'(0)=1, so no one located source has its exact two-part packaging.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-57453--{"id":"lem-scaled-binomial-coefficients-converge","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_logandexp.html","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch10.pdf"],"rationale":"This fixed-k coefficient limit and 0<=product<=1 bound are the standard coefficient calculation underlying binomial proofs of (1+x/n)^n -> e^x. The located sources state that product limit and the binomial machinery, but not this extracted lemma verbatim; the finite-product derivation is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-57454-+{"id":"lem-scaled-binomial-coefficients-converge","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_logandexp.html","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch10.pdf","https://aofa.cs.princeton.edu/40asymptotic/"],"rationale":"Princeton states for fixed k that binom(N,k)=N^k/k!(1+O(1/N)), which is semantically the exact asserted limit. Lebl and Hunter supply the surrounding product-limit and binomial context. The displayed finite-product proof and its additional bound in [0,1/k!] are local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log:57455: {"id":"thm-exponential-product-limit","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_logandexp.html","https://people.math.wisc.edu/~hkeisler/foundations.pdf"],"rationale":"Lebl Exercise 5.4.5 states e^x=lim_n(1+x/n)^n for every real x, with the same eventual-domain convention implicit in a real sequence. The library supplies a binomial head-tail proof instead of Lebl's logarithmic hint.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-57456- {"id":"thm-picard-iterates-for-exponential","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_picard.html","https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~ancoop/3600/section-34.html"],"rationale":"Lebl's Picard example for y'=y, y(0)=1 gives the iterates 1+x+...+x^n/n! and their global limit exp. The item additionally records compact-uniform convergence and the limiting integral equation, so it is a faithful strengthened packaging; its induction and interchange proof adapt the standard construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-audit-beta-a4.log-57457- {"id":"thm-exponential-definition-equivalence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www2.math.upenn.edu/~ancoop/3600/section-34.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_picard.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_logandexp.html"],"rationale":"The sources identify the ODE, factorial power series, product-limit, functional-equation, and Picard descriptions of the ordinary exponential across their sections. The item is a library-specific consolidation of five standard characterizations, and its proof is the local composition of the preceding equivalence results.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
